  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 68-year-old woman presents to her GP with a 3-year history of worsening right hip pain, worse on walking and at the end of the day, with morning stiffness lasting less than 15 minutes. She has a BMI of 31 and works as a school teacher. Examination shows reduced internal rotation of the right hip with pain at the extremes of movement. She has tried regular paracetamol and topical NSAIDs with minimal benefit and is struggling to walk to work.',
  'What is the most appropriate next investigation?',
  array['osteoarthritis','hip pain','plain radiograph']
),
